      "kind": "site history",
      "description": "The San Francisco chapter of the National Council of Negro Women opened its headquarters here in September 1956 and ran its Citizenship Education Project from the building — a two-phase voter registration and education drive with a sample voting machine installed on the premises. Identified in 2024 as eligible for local landmark, California Register or National Register designation.",
